  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on comparing maximum outcomes (and minimum if tied), favoring the lottery with the higher maximum outcome. In this case, Lottery A has a higher maximum (4000 > 3000), so the reason would favor A. However, the individual chose B and justified the choice based on certainty and guaranteed payoff, not on the magnitude of the maximum or minimum outcomes. The individual did not consider outcome differences in the way the reason prescribes; instead, the focus was on probability (certainty). Therefore, the information considered (certainty of outcome) and the justification (preference for guaranteed payoff) do not align with the decision reason, which ignores probabilities and focuses solely on outcome levels. There is no indication that the individual compared maximum or minimum outcomes as per the reason.",
